rephrase commit message keep style and action verbs
commit header epxected under 50 chars
rephrase such that commit message explains the reason why changes were comitted 
sentences starts with action verbs as if saying "this commit [verb]"
but do not write "this commit" only verb at third person for example
"this commit includes..." -> "Includes..."
draft to rephrase is enclosed in <draft>...</draft> tags

<draft>
{{.Stdin}}
</draft>

for the header message ask yourself
**What kind of change is it?** Pick the most appropriate type:
   - **feat** – new feature / user-visible functionality
   - **fix** – bug correction / regression fix
   - **docs** – documentation only
   - **style** – formatting, whitespace, lint fixes (no code change)
   - **refactor** – internal restructuring, no functional change
   - **perf** – performance improvement
   - **test** – adding/changing tests only
   - **chore** – build, CI, tooling, or other maintenance
Write a commit header ≤50 chars using “change(context): summary”.
